WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.290
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:05.290 --> 00:00:06.470
SPEAKER: Hello.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:08.140
We often get questions
from companies

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.180
about how to
document and transfer

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.440
their API program's knowledge
across attributed teams.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.660
Enter the API Playbook.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.760
The API Playbook is
a living document

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:22.060
that guides the overall
direction of your API program.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.430
When we consider the
digital value chain,

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.940
every aspect is an integral
part of the API Playbook.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:31.510
For example, how do you
ensure your APIs are secure?

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:34.420
What processes will you have in
place to connect your back end

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:37.630
services to your applications?

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.480
And how will you engage
your community and customers

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.450
to ensure your API
program is successful?

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:46.720
These questions and others
all need to be answered.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:48.340
The playbook describes
your approach

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:50.380
to API management as a whole.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:53.110
It includes the essential
standards that all APIs must

00:00:53.110 --> 00:00:56.050
follow for an organization,
the best practices

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.670
for designing APIs, in a common
and consumer friendly fashion,

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:02.770
and the essential
ways of working

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:07.420
for API producing teams to
boost quality APIs at speed

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:08.830
and scale.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:12.250
Your playbook should
focus on six key areas,

00:01:12.250 --> 00:01:16.210
your organization, best
practices, API design

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:19.780
decisions, development
requirements, API management

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.830
and deployment processes, and
overall support guidelines.

00:01:23.830 --> 00:01:25.600
This should be a
living document,

00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:28.000
derived from industry
best practices,

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.060
and best of all, experience
of people inside your company.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:34.360
Here's a condensed
summary of various items

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.760
that will appear in a playbook.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:38.500
Every business is unique.

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.840
And as a result,
every API Playbook

00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:43.890
is also unique to that business.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:47.260
Let's take a closer look
at the core topics and what

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:50.120
information you may
find in each section.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.020
In this section, APIs
in your organization

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:56.320
explains how API governance,
ownership, and federation

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:57.310
works.

00:01:57.310 --> 00:02:01.420
It's important to stress who
and how APIs will be managed

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.970
as well as what types of APIs
are in your organization,

00:02:04.970 --> 00:02:08.110
as well as what API teams
and roles should be,

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.759
and what they do.

00:02:09.759 --> 00:02:13.060
Your guideline and guiding
principle to follow here

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:16.840
is as you move towards a
comprehensive API program,

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:20.440
you should have an API first
mandate from leadership.

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:23.650
Direct your digital product
owners and API teams

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:27.400
to own their APIs and leverage
a common infrastructure

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.440
with common design
patterns that flow

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:31.540
throughout the
entire organization.

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.193
Successful APIs require
more than good technology.

00:02:35.193 --> 00:02:36.610
You'll need to
ensure your team is

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:40.330
equipped with the right
people and processes.

00:02:40.330 --> 00:02:43.630
Traditional development
processes, or waterfall project

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.820
management, simply
doesn't work when

00:02:45.820 --> 00:02:48.220
a team has to respond to
opportunities, feedback,

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.230
or problems quickly.

00:02:50.230 --> 00:02:52.300
This section covers
best practices

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:55.870
for organization using
agile development for APIs.

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:58.390
Outline your software
development lifecycle,

00:02:58.390 --> 00:03:00.670
how your teams will
maintain quality assurance,

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:03.700
and what strategies you'll
focus on for mocking your data,

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:07.180
and how all of these ways of
working might be automated.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:09.100
Your guiding principle
here is simple.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.860
Successful teams
are agile, nimble,

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:14.260
and leverage automation.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:16.570
And a large enterprise,
many different lines

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:20.380
of businesses and API teams
will be producing APIs.

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:23.560
And it's a slippery slope
of discordant design

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:27.340
if we don't all follow
the similar guidelines.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:30.280
This section details the
important aspects of your API

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:33.760
design and helps to
guide a consistent look

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:38.650
and feel and function of all
the APIs in your catalog.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:42.760
Your guiding principle, your API
should be designed as products

00:03:42.760 --> 00:03:44.800
with an outside
in view, allowing

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:48.250
developers and consumers to
easily read and understand

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.720
your data.

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.240
In the development section
of your API playbook,

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:55.180
document how you'll
facilitate security as well

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:57.310
as other patterns
and policies which

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:59.500
are required in the enterprise.

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:03.010
Provide guidance on how user
authentication will be managed

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.470
as well as any other
policies for logging,

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.770
transformation,
or orchestration.

00:04:08.770 --> 00:04:11.200
These are often mandatory
development guidelines

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:15.930
regardless of what the
functionality the API exposes.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:19.620
You're guiding principle here
is to provide reusable shared

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:22.350
flows, assets,
and other patterns

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:26.400
designed to help your API
teams go to market faster.

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:28.950
In this section, we
detailed the configurations

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:32.520
necessary for a successful
pathway to production.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:35.580
It should outline each step
of your continuous integration

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:38.850
and delivery process
and the tools used.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:41.430
Furthermore, it list
each environment and what

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:43.200
that environment is used for.

00:04:43.200 --> 00:04:45.510
You can also include
lists of analytics reports

00:04:45.510 --> 00:04:48.780
that will help support
auditing, governance, marketing,

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:51.043
and ongoing development.

00:04:51.043 --> 00:04:52.710
You should also include
steps to prepare

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:56.280
technical and non-technical
documentation for the developer

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:57.150
portal.

00:04:57.150 --> 00:05:00.150
Your guiding principle here
is your software development

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:02.160
lifecycle should
be tightly coupled

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.800
with continuous
integration and delivery

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.520
tools that manage your APIs
from coding, to deployment,

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:11.220
to monitoring, and analysis.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:14.400
In your support section, explain
how your developer portal

00:05:14.400 --> 00:05:16.510
will be used to manage.

00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:18.610
Discuss how you will
support your community

00:05:18.610 --> 00:05:21.760
with documentation around
FAQs, troubleshooting,

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:25.690
support steps, and resources you
might make available to them.

00:05:25.690 --> 00:05:28.520
Investing the time to
create a good resource

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:30.730
and support workflows
will pay dividends

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.440
when it comes to
both your customers

00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:35.230
and your own
organization's time.

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:39.850
Your guiding principle, your
consumers are your customers.

00:05:39.850 --> 00:05:42.850
And a good customer experience
is a critical factor

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:44.800
for building useful APIs.

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:46.750
A thriving community
will ultimately

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:50.860
help your API program to
grow and become successful.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:53.200
Hopefully, you now
have a solid outline

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.350
to build your
first API Playbook.

00:05:56.350 --> 00:05:58.450
If you want more
information, please check out

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.850
the community for
ebooks, articles,

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:02.952
and other related topics.

00:06:02.952 --> 00:06:03.910
Thank you for watching.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:06.060
[MUSIC PLAYING]

